From 5db31996da5cc7e9307efc928383f646a820d77c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: stephan-xyz <stephan@zehrer.xyz>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 07:29:52 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] netstack: SLAAC with every prefix of a router advertisement

smoltcp keeps only the last prefix option of a router advertisement, so
with a global and a unique local prefix (Fritz!Box) only the unique local
address was formed (Pi tests #47, #55). The options are now read from the
raw message: one address per autonomous /64 prefix, global ones first,
removed when the valid lifetime drops to 0. A router lifetime of 0 ends
only the router that sent it, so an advertisement from another router
no longer drops the default route.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
